            "## Ideas That Spread",
            "Mason's words did not stay in Virginia. Thomas Jefferson, who was writing the Declaration of Independence in Philadelphia that same summer, borrowed ideas from Mason's work. Several years later, Mason's ideas helped shape the Bill of Rights, the first ten amendments to the U.S. Constitution.",
