            "Mason's ideas about freedom were powerful, but they did not apply to everyone in his own time. Like many Virginia planters, Mason enslaved people, even though he criticized slavery and warned that it harmed the nation. Historians today study this contradiction as they work to tell a full and honest history of the founding era.",
